<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ethiopian Red Terror</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1976–1978</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Qey Shibir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ethiopian Red Terror was a campaign of violent repression waged by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> military government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu Haile Mariam</a>, at its height in 1977-1978. Aimed chiefly at the Ethiopian People's Revolutionary Party and other leftist rivals, it involved mass arrests, torture and public displays of the dead. Tens of thousands of people were killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ethiopian-red-terror.jpg" alt="Ethiopian Red Terror" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Insights Unspoken · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Terror_Martyrs_Memorial_Museum,_Addis_Ababa_(26854504685).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
